sentences.text:
On perusal of Ex.P5-wound certificate, it is seen that the claimant has sustained:
i) Abrasion over the face lateral to (L) eye 2" x 1";
ii) Small lacerated wound below (L) knee;
iii) Deformity (L) leg 1/3rd.
(b) The tribunal has awarded a sum of Rs.30,000/-
under the head pain and suffering, which is on the lower side.

Accordingly, I pass the following :
ORDER Sri Fayaz Khan vs Sri Javid Pasha on 18 January, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/29066256/
4 i) The appeal is allowed-in-part;

ii) The judgment and award passed by Senior Civil Judge & XIV Motor Accident Claims Tribunal, Tiptur in MVC.No.672/2011 dated 04.01.2014, is modified;
iii) The claimant is entitled for total compensation of `1,29,500/- as against `62,600/- awarded by the tribunal;
iv) In view of the fact that respondent-owner of the offending vehicle has already satisfied the decreetal amount, the balance amount awarded by this Court shall also be paid/deposited by the respondent-owner of the offending vehicle along with interest @ 6% from the date of petition till realisation, within a period of eight weeks from the date of the judgment.

